#!/bin/sh
# Repo gate — wired as BOTH pre-commit and pre-push (identical bytes).
# Runs the same fail-loud check CI runs (.github/workflows/ci.yml, `surface` job).
#
# Enable once per clone — git deliberately refuses to let a repo configure its
# own hooks, so the files travel with the clone but the pointer does not:
#   git config core.hooksPath .githooks
#
# Fails CLOSED on purpose: a missing node or a missing script blocks the commit
# instead of passing quietly.
#
# Only the surface check runs here, deliberately. CI's other two gates are wrong
# for a hook: the brand byte-identity gate REGENERATES assets, so it would write
# files in the middle of a commit, and the post-deploy check needs the network
# and a deploy that has not happened yet. This hook moves the room's own laws
# earlier; it does not try to be CI.
node scripts/surface-check.mjs
